{
 "_about": "World colour tokens. DESIGN.md L1788-1803 (swatches), L1801 (boot-topping, antifouling), L1941 (primer), L1917 (island bands), L1857-1872 (presets: sun, sky, ambient floor, fog, exposure), L1846 and L1824 (LUT grades, no teal-orange), L1953 (VFX ramps). The only place a world colour may be written. Each colour is authored as linear luminance Y plus a small OKLCH chroma and hue; OKLCH lightness is solved so luminance equals Y (chroma drops first if the sRGB gamut clips), then linear RGB, sRGB and CIE L* are derived. Munsell notation is authored and checked against Y by ASTM D1535. Written by `cargo xtask tokens` from crates/xtask/src/art/tokens.rs (unit xt-art-tokens); never edit by hand.",
